<title>RUSSIA: Interfax says Lebed may be sacked.</title>
<headline>Interfax says Lebed may be sacked.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interfax news agency said on Thursday that Russian security chief Alexander Lebed could be sacked &quot;in the near future&quot;.</p>
<p>But Interfax said it had not been able to confirm its information, which it said came from informed sources. President Boris Yeltsin is expected to appear on television at 1400 GMT.</p>
</text>
